    "title": "pandas.api.types.is_iterator — pandas 3.1.0.dev0+1386.gcb2086a1a4 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.api.types.is_iterator#\n\n- \npandas.api.types.is_iterator(*obj* )#\n- Check if the object is an iterator. This is intended for generators, not list-like objects. This method checks whether the passed object is an iterator. It returns True if the object is an iterator, and False otherwise. \n  - Parameters:\n    - **obj** The object to check\n    - The object to check for iterator type.\n  - Returns:\n    - **is_iter** bool\n    - Whether obj is an iterator. True if the object is of iterator type, otherwise False.\n See also \n  - `api.types.is_list_like`\n  - Check if the input is list-like.\n Examples >>> import datetime >>> from pandas.api.types import is_iterator >>> is_iterator((x for x in [])) True >>> is_iterator([1, 2, 3]) False >>> is_iterator(datetime.datetime(2017, 1, 1)) False >>> is_iterator(\"foo\") False >>> is_iterator(1) False",
